  "notes": "Drawn from 2025-2026 photos of N8646B. The wreath is described, not drawn. Belly: cobalt as far as the photos show (the underside is not seen squarely). Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One (the same fin on every 737), copied with its 'Southwest' title and flag. 'Nevada One' measured on the June 2025 left photo against the nose and the forward door (1.9-2.9 m back), two weights, a pair of titles per side (the right mirrored; the 2026 right photo shows it in the same place but too small to measure), on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows. The 'Battle Born' scroll's curved edges made smooth, its cut end kept square. 'NEVADA' and 'BATTLE BORN' follow curves on the aircraft; drawn level; NEVADA's length (0.04, about 1.6 m) measured on the June 2025 photo between the door and the overwing exits.",
  "history": "Previously N727SW (1999)."
